#: src/Admin/Pages/AboutPage.php:1941
msgid "A native browser validation failure — field id, field type, and which <code>ValidityState</code> flag failed. <strong>Never the value typed.</strong>"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Pages/AboutPage.php:1942
msgid "A submit attempt. Success unconfirmed. Carries the attempt's conversion token in <code>event_value</code>, which is how the confirmed success is ordered after it."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Pages/AboutPage.php:1943
msgid "A confirmed conversion, carrying the <code>conversion_id</code> in <code>event_value</code>."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Pages/AboutPage.php:1944
msgid "Configurable dwell time; opt-in per element via <code>data-cvmtry-hover</code>."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Pages/AboutPage.php:1945
msgid "50% and 100% milestones."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Pages/AboutPage.php:1946
msgid "A named event from <code>Convermetry.track()</code>, kept only when a goal matches its name."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Pages/AboutPage.php:1947
msgid "<strong>Delivery reliability.</strong> Batches flush every 5 seconds, at 20 events, and on page exit via <code>navigator.sendBeacon</code>. Page fields are cut to the width the server stores, and a flush that would still pass the endpoint's 64 KB limit is split across several requests. Every batch is persisted to a bounded <code>sessionStorage</code> store <em>before</em> it is sent and removed only on server acknowledgment. Failed sends back off exponentially with jitter; a 429 pauses the whole tab and honors <code>Retry-After</code>. Delivery is <strong>at-least-once</strong> and replays are <strong>idempotent</strong> — rows are stored under a unique (batch id, event ordinal) key, so a replayed batch never inflates counts."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Pages/AboutPage.php:1948
msgid "<strong>Endpoint defenses.</strong> Whitelisted, currently-enabled event types only; tracked page URLs must be <code>http(s)</code> on this site's host and are canonicalized to scheme + host + path; foreign <code>Origin</code>/<code>Referer</code> rejected; bots and empty user agents ignored — matched by how a crawler, headless browser or scripted client names itself, so a handset such as a CUBOT is not mistaken for one; DNT/GPC enforced server-side when enabled; request bodies and batch sizes capped; scalar-only field values, sanitized and truncated; rate limits charged <strong>per event</strong> — 300 per IP per minute plus 3,000 site-wide — via atomic object-cache counters, falling back (and failing <strong>closed</strong>) to an atomic single-statement database counter. The per-IP check runs first, so a flooding IP never consumes the site-wide budget."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Pages/AboutPage.php:1949
msgid "<strong>Sessions are cookie-free.</strong> The id lives in <code>localStorage</code> and rotates after 30 minutes of inactivity."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Pages/AboutPage.php:1953
msgid "Campaign and channel attribution"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Pages/AboutPage.php:1955
msgid "All six UTM parameters (<code>utm_source</code>, <code>utm_medium</code>, <code>utm_campaign</code>, <code>utm_id</code>, <code>utm_term</code>, <code>utm_content</code>) are captured from tagged landing URLs. Ad-click identifiers (<code>gclid</code>, <code>gbraid</code>, <code>wbraid</code>, <code>fbclid</code>, <code>msclkid</code>, <code>ttclid</code>, <code>twclid</code>, <code>li_fat_id</code>) are recognized — only the parameter <strong>name</strong> is stored, never the value — and imply source/medium when no UTM tags are present."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Pages/AboutPage.php:1956
msgid "Attribution is <strong>last-touch within the session</strong>: the most recent tagged landing attributes the visit from that point on, and the snapshot rides on <em>every</em> event in the session. Untagged acquisition persists too — the session's entrance referrer travels alongside (with an explicit marker for verified direct entrances), so organic, social and referral visits keep their channel across internal navigation."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Pages/AboutPage.php:1957
msgid "<strong>Channels</strong> — every attributed event is classified at ingestion into: Paid Search, Paid Social, Organic Search, Organic Social, Email, Display, Affiliate, SMS, Referral, Direct, Other. There is exactly <strong>one</strong> attribution engine: the dashboard, the analytics payloads, every goal completion, and every form submission's <code>analytics_context.channel</code> classify through the same code, so they cannot disagree. Source aliases are normalized (<code>convermetry_source_aliases</code>) and the result is overridable per event (<code>convermetry_channel</code>)."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Pages/AboutPage.php:1961
msgid "Session → submission → conversion correlation"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Pages/AboutPage.php:1963
msgid "The link between analytics and leads is <strong>token-based — never timestamps</strong>."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Pages/AboutPage.php:1965
msgid "On page load, and again at submit time in the capture phase <em>before</em> any AJAX handler serializes the form, the tracker injects three hidden fields: <code>cvmtry_conversion_id</code> (a fresh token per submission attempt), <code>cvmtry_session_id</code>, and <code>cvmtry_context</code> (a compact JSON snapshot of attribution, entrance referrer, landing page, and page URL). Only into a submission that is really a same-origin <code>POST</code>: method and destination are read as the browser reads them, a <code>&lt;base href&gt;</code> and the pressed button's <code>formaction</code> / <code>formmethod</code> count, and fields already injected are taken back out of a submission that goes anywhere else."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Pages/AboutPage.php:1966
msgid "The form plugin processes the submission normally. When its <strong>server-side success hook</strong> fires, Convermetry's adapter extracts and strictly validates those fields — every transport shape is handled, including Fluent Forms' serialized <code>data</code> blob — and <strong>strips every <code>cvmtry_*</code> field</strong> from the lead data."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Pages/AboutPage.php:1967
msgid "The confirmed conversion is recorded as a <code>form_success</code> analytics event under that same token, together with a durable submission row."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Pages/AboutPage.php:1968
msgid "The tracker's own frontend success listeners reuse the <strong>same token</strong>, so whichever paths fire, every report deduplicates them into <strong>one</strong> conversion."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Pages/AboutPage.php:1969
msgid "AJAX forms are fully supported. When the fields are absent — tracker disabled, privacy signals honored, JavaScript blocked, server-to-server submissions — the conversion id is generated on the server and the submission still records and delivers, just with an empty <code>analytics_context</code>. Its <code>form_success</code> event takes the page from a same-site <code>Referer</code> and has no channel, matching the lead: with no tracker there is no evidence of how the visitor arrived, so neither claims Direct. The channel report lists those conversions under a blank channel. No cookies are used at any point."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Pages/AboutPage.php:1970
msgid "<strong>Duplicate protection at every layer:</strong> a double-fired provider callback hits the <code>UNIQUE conversion_id</code> index and records nothing twice; queue rows are unique per (submission, endpoint); reports count <code>DISTINCT conversion_id</code>; receivers deduplicate by <code>delivery_id</code>."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Pages/AboutPage.php:1986
msgid "Four things beyond the conversion count"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Pages/AboutPage.php:1989
msgid "<strong>Goals</strong> count important actions that are not form submissions: a phone number tapped, a PDF opened, a booking link followed, a pricing page reached."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Pages/AboutPage.php:1990
msgid "<strong>Funnels</strong> measure the ordered path to a conversion — how many sessions reached each step and how many were lost between them."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Pages/AboutPage.php:1991
msgid "<strong>Form engagement</strong> reports views, starts, attempts, successes and abandonment per form, plus which fields fail validation most often."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Pages/AboutPage.php:1992
msgid "<strong>Lead status and value</strong> record what a submission turned out to be worth, so campaign reporting can be measured against outcomes rather than treating every conversion as equal."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Pages/AboutPage.php:1998
msgid "<strong>A confirmed form submission is not a goal.</strong> A submission is <em>server-confirmed</em> — the form plugin's own success hook said so. A goal completion is a <em>browser-observed</em> signal. They are stored in different tables and counted separately on purpose: folding submissions into goals would quietly downgrade the plugin's most trustworthy number to the standard of its least."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Pages/AboutPage.php:1999
msgid "<strong>Matching happens on the server</strong>, at ingestion, against data the tracker already sends. The browser is never told what your goals are. Three consequences:"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Pages/AboutPage.php:2001
msgid "Your list of valuable actions is competitive information and stays on the server."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Pages/AboutPage.php:2002
msgid "<strong>Phone and email goals need no configuration at all.</strong> The tracker already reports click destinations and keeps <code>tel:</code> and <code>mailto:</code> URLs whole while stripping query strings from everything else — pick \"on a phone number link\" and you are done. No CSS selector required."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Pages/AboutPage.php:2003
msgid "A visitor cannot manufacture a conversion by claiming one. They can only report the same raw activity any visitor reports; the server decides what it means."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Pages/AboutPage.php:2004
msgid "The one exception is a <strong>CSS selector</strong>, which genuinely cannot be evaluated without the DOM. Only those selectors are sent to the tracker, and the goal ids it reports back are re-validated against your enabled selector goals before anything is recorded."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Pages/AboutPage.php:2005
msgid "Goal type"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Pages/AboutPage.php:2005
#: src/Admin/Pages/AboutPage.php:2551
msgid "Rules"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Pages/AboutPage.php:2006
#: src/Admin/Pages/GoalsPage.php:944
msgid "Reaching a page"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Pages/AboutPage.php:2006
msgid "is exactly · contains · starts with · ends with. A path (<code>/thank-you/</code>) matches the URL's path; a full URL matches the whole URL. Trailing slashes are forgiven and matching is case-insensitive."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Pages/AboutPage.php:2007
#: src/Admin/Pages/GoalsPage.php:943
msgid "A click"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Pages/AboutPage.php:2007
msgid "on a phone number link · on an email link · that leaves this site · where the link contains / is exactly · matching a CSS selector. A phone tap is deliberately <strong>not</strong> also counted as an external link."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Pages/AboutPage.php:2008
msgid "A custom event"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Pages/AboutPage.php:2008
msgid "Matched by name, fired from your own code with <code>Convermetry.track('name')</code>."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Pages/AboutPage.php:2009
msgid "<strong>Counting.</strong> Each goal counts either <em>once per visit</em> or <em>every occurrence</em>, and deduplication is enforced by a <strong>UNIQUE database constraint</strong> rather than a PHP check — so an at-least-once replay of a tracker batch collides with the original instead of double-counting."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Pages/AboutPage.php:2010
msgid "<strong>Editing.</strong> A goal keeps its id forever. Editing its <em>matching rule</em> starts a new measurement series (and reports say the definition changed) so two different questions are never blended into one line. Renaming, pausing, or repricing a goal resets nothing. Removing one is a soft delete: past completions are kept and still appear, correctly labelled, in reports for earlier periods. Goals count from when you create them and are never applied retroactively."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Pages/AboutPage.php:2011
msgid "Goals do <strong>not</strong> override the tracking toggles they depend on — a click goal cannot fire while click tracking is off. Silently re-enabling tracking you switched off would be the wrong fix, so the Goals screen names the specific setting and links to it instead."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Pages/AboutPage.php:2030
msgid "Step types: <strong>visited a page</strong>, <strong>completed a goal</strong>, <strong>saw a form</strong>, <strong>started filling a form</strong>, <strong>attempted to submit</strong>, and <strong>submission confirmed by the form plugin</strong>. A form step with no specific form counts any form on the site."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Pages/AboutPage.php:2031
msgid "<strong>Ordering is real.</strong> Steps must occur in sequence — a session that reached step three without step two is not counted at step three. Each step is constrained to occur strictly after the previous one, because the naive approach gets this wrong in a way that looks right on small data:"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Pages/AboutPage.php:2037
msgid "Ordering uses the event id rather than the timestamp: the events table's <code>created_at</code> is the moment the row was <em>inserted</em>, so the two are the same order by construction and the id is the finer, tie-free version of it. A consequence worth knowing: funnel order is <em>ingestion</em> order. Within one batch the browser's order is preserved; a batch that failed and was resent from a later page sorts by when it arrived."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Pages/AboutPage.php:2038
msgid "<strong>One exception, and it is causal.</strong> A confirmed <code>form_success</code> is written by the form plugin's own request, while the browser's attempt travels separately, and either can be stored first. Every attempt carries its conversion token, so a confirmed success is placed <strong>no earlier than the attempt with the same token</strong> in the same session. No timestamp is consulted and nothing else moves. Events recorded before 1.1.2 carry no token and keep their ingestion order."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Pages/AboutPage.php:2039
msgid "Sessions with no session id are excluded — an empty session id is not one visitor, it is every visitor whose session could not be established, and grouping on it would produce one enormous pseudo-session that appears to complete every funnel."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Pages/AboutPage.php:2040
msgid "<strong>Cohorts.</strong> A funnel is the set of sessions that reached step 1 during the selected period. Later steps are counted for up to <strong>24 hours past the end of the period</strong>, so a session that entered at 23:55 on the last day is not unfairly cut off. Each funnel's result is cached for five minutes, keyed by its definition, so editing a step invalidates the cache automatically. Limits: 8 steps per funnel, 20 funnels per site."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Pages/AboutPage.php:2044
msgid "Form engagement & abandonment"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Pages/AboutPage.php:2046
msgid "Mixing units here would make every rate meaningless and the mix would be invisible, so each column states its unit and its evidence:"
msgstr ""

