#: src/Admin/Pages/AboutPage.php:2117
msgid "Per-form settings key by the provider's own most stable form identity. <strong>Two providers are opt in per form</strong> — Elementor Atomic and Bricks Builder both run an explicit list of actions after submit, so a form of theirs captures nothing until the Convermetry action is selected in that builder's editor. Convermetry never edits saved builder content to add it, and cannot tell from the outside which forms have it; the <strong>Forms</strong> page says so beside those rows. Custom forms integrate through the <a href=\"#developer\">public API</a>, and third-party adapters register with the <a href=\"#hook-convermetry_form_providers\"><code>convermetry_form_providers</code></a> filter."
